WEBVTT

00:06.910 --> 00:08.690
I apologize for the other day.

00:09.650 --> 00:11.290
What business do you have here?

00:11.290 --> 00:13.470
I heard from Mr. Evan that you were facing

00:13.470 --> 00:15.910
a really difficult situation 
of some kind at the time.

00:17.070 --> 00:18.880
Are you here to ask about the abbey again?

00:18.880 --> 00:19.620
Not at all.

00:19.950 --> 00:22.060
The village head didn't know anything either,

00:22.060 --> 00:24.670
so it looks like I had come 
on a wild goose chase.

00:24.670 --> 00:25.920
Is that so?

00:25.920 --> 00:28.540
So, we've decided to continue on our journey,

00:28.540 --> 00:32.360
and we've come to the church 
to pray for safe travels.

00:45.140 --> 00:52.860
Spice and Wolf

02:04.130 --> 02:05.180
This way.

02:05.390 --> 02:09.400
<b>Episode 22
Church Teachings and
Memories of Father</b>

02:09.170 --> 02:11.130
Then, a prayer...

02:11.130 --> 02:12.320
Father Franz.

02:12.320 --> 02:12.860
Huh?

02:12.860 --> 02:15.480
He must have been a man of great faith.

02:16.650 --> 02:17.530
Oh.

02:18.360 --> 02:21.020
Yes, he was.

02:21.020 --> 02:21.740
Just...

02:22.080 --> 02:24.540
I hadn't noticed until you pointed it out. {Note: She's talking about the worn floor where it seems Father Franz had kneeled to pray.}

02:27.220 --> 02:29.010
Now, let us pray.

02:29.010 --> 02:31.810
Oh, before that, I'd like to make a confession.

02:31.810 --> 02:32.840
I see.

02:34.440 --> 02:36.260
Then let us go into a different room...

02:36.260 --> 02:37.580
No, I'd like to do it here.

02:37.580 --> 02:39.510
Before God, if possible.

02:40.390 --> 02:41.510
I understand.

02:44.220 --> 02:48.300
Let God hear your confession, for He...

02:53.020 --> 02:55.650
is gracious to those who are honest with Him.

02:57.250 --> 02:59.060
I have lied.

02:59.450 --> 03:02.480
I have fooled another for my own gain.

03:02.480 --> 03:06.520
Do you have the courage 
to confess the truth before God?

03:06.520 --> 03:07.450
I do.

03:07.450 --> 03:09.440
There is no need to be afraid.

03:09.440 --> 03:13.280
God is merciful to those who are faithful.

03:13.280 --> 03:15.420
I lied today.

03:15.810 --> 03:18.920
I spoke falsely to trick another.

03:19.310 --> 03:20.560
For what reason?

03:20.560 --> 03:22.480
There was something I needed to know.

03:22.480 --> 03:24.580
I lied in order to get close 
to the other person.

03:25.110 --> 03:28.190
Who did you lie to?

03:28.190 --> 03:29.430
You, Ms. Elsa.

03:30.060 --> 03:35.830
I have confessed my lies before God.

03:35.830 --> 03:37.890
And now, I shall speak the truth.

03:37.890 --> 03:41.490
I have come to ask about 
the location of Diendran Abbey.

03:42.580 --> 03:45.220
No, I have lied again.

03:45.220 --> 03:47.400
I have not come to ask for the location.

03:47.400 --> 03:48.270
Huh?

03:48.270 --> 03:51.910
Ms. Elsa, I came to confirm that 
this place is Diendran Abbey.

03:53.850 --> 03:59.020
And, Father Franz is also known as 
the managing abbot, Louis Lana Schtinghilt.

03:59.020 --> 04:00.550
Am I wrong?

04:00.950 --> 04:02.760
You are before God.

04:03.090 --> 04:05.070
You must not lie before Him.

04:05.800 --> 04:10.180
We have come to ask about the stories 
of pagan gods he had collected.

04:11.370 --> 04:16.770
You are worried about the town of Enberch 
discovering the actions of Father Franz, right?

04:17.790 --> 04:21.240
Wh-Who in the world are you two?!

04:21.240 --> 04:27.120
It is difficult to give you a satisfying 
answer to that question.

04:27.120 --> 04:28.880
D-Difficult?

04:28.880 --> 04:30.540
This is the reason.

04:35.210 --> 04:37.480
Do you wish to touch them?

04:44.860 --> 04:47.330
She is much more timid than I expected.

04:47.330 --> 04:48.640
I wonder about that.

04:48.970 --> 04:53.770
That letter was from a lord of another area 
stating he would support this church.

04:54.220 --> 04:56.410
She must've been busy 
every night until its arrival.

04:57.710 --> 05:01.190
It seems that things are a lot more 
dire here than I imagined.

05:05.000 --> 05:05.990
Are you all right?

05:09.980 --> 05:11.830
So, it wasn't a dream.

05:12.330 --> 05:15.040
Though it would be better 
for you to think as such.

05:15.370 --> 05:18.290
They say devils fool humans in their dreams.

05:20.830 --> 05:25.090
Once we finish what we came here for, 
we will disappear like a dream.

05:25.800 --> 05:29.560
There should be records of 
the stories Father Franz collected.

05:29.560 --> 05:31.330
Why are you looking for such a thing?

05:31.330 --> 05:33.140
I wish to return home.

05:33.560 --> 05:34.690
Home?

05:34.690 --> 05:37.840
I left my hometown ages ago.

05:37.840 --> 05:41.770
I have forgotten my way back and do not 
know if my friends are still doing well.

05:42.190 --> 05:46.340
Moreover, I am not even sure 
whether my hometown still exists.

05:46.340 --> 05:47.700
What would you do?

05:48.620 --> 05:52.580
If you knew there was someone 
who may know about your home, long lost?

05:57.580 --> 05:59.670
I am a servant of God.

06:01.860 --> 06:05.640
At the same time, I am someone who 
wishes to follow Father Franz's footsteps.

06:05.640 --> 06:08.300
I do not believe you have been 
possessed by the devil.

06:08.750 --> 06:12.680
Father Franz always said there is 
no such thing as being possessed by the devil.

06:14.430 --> 06:15.710
Please follow me.

06:36.840 --> 06:38.320
What is this place?

06:38.590 --> 06:42.480
Precious things are always 
hidden behind the prayer room.

06:43.150 --> 06:45.130
May God forgive us.

06:52.550 --> 06:57.460
In his will, Father Franz wrote that the 
statue could then be removed from its place...

06:57.460 --> 06:58.650
I understand.

07:00.330 --> 07:01.950
There we go.

07:06.410 --> 07:08.030
May we enter?

07:08.840 --> 07:10.250
I will go first.

07:17.910 --> 07:19.070
Be careful.

07:24.130 --> 07:26.650
She's not going to set fire to 
the basement, is she?

07:26.650 --> 07:29.630
You are much more suspicious than I.

07:34.010 --> 07:36.770
Thank you for waiting.

07:36.770 --> 07:37.430
Not at all.

07:37.740 --> 07:38.810
What are those?

07:38.810 --> 07:39.730
Letters.

07:40.130 --> 07:41.650
To me.

07:41.650 --> 07:43.790
There are books in the basement.

07:43.790 --> 07:46.370
I believe they are what you are looking for.

07:46.370 --> 07:48.090
May we take them out and read them?

07:48.090 --> 07:50.580
Please read them within the church.

07:55.400 --> 07:57.770
I know we forced you to do this.

07:57.770 --> 08:00.210
I'd like to thank you, as well as apologize.

08:00.210 --> 08:02.900
Yes, you did indeed force me.

08:03.550 --> 08:04.640
However...

08:05.390 --> 08:07.960
I'm sure Father Franz would have been happy.

08:08.300 --> 08:13.310
He always said that the stories 
he collected were not mere fairy tales...

08:15.380 --> 08:17.350
It's just, I did not expect so many books...

08:17.640 --> 08:21.880
You may need to talk with the inn about 
staying a few more days to read them all.

08:21.880 --> 08:25.210
But you might call for help in that time.

08:25.210 --> 08:28.340
I have spent my life embracing the true faith.

08:28.340 --> 08:30.480
I would never lay a trap for others.

08:30.810 --> 08:34.660
Even in the prayer room, I did not lie.

08:34.660 --> 08:37.990
Yes, I was the one who laid a trap for you.

08:39.150 --> 08:42.490
I'll remember that you should never 
let your guard down around a merchant.

08:46.850 --> 08:48.190
Hey...

08:50.420 --> 08:52.650
May I read these here?

08:52.650 --> 08:55.590
You may, but remember to extinguish 
the candles when you're finished.

08:55.590 --> 08:58.200
This is not a wealthy church.

08:58.200 --> 08:59.100
Very well.

09:04.830 --> 09:09.900
If a merchant wishes to ascend to heaven, 
I heard that he needs to lighten his purse.

09:11.020 --> 09:12.320
Thank you.

09:14.350 --> 09:16.650
May God's blessing be with you.

09:18.440 --> 09:20.200
You don't need to watch over us?

09:20.200 --> 09:24.670
As you don't plan to bring disaster upon 
our village, I have no reason to make a fuss.

09:24.670 --> 09:29.210
True, your companion is a being 
that should not be in this church.

09:29.210 --> 09:30.210
However...

09:30.210 --> 09:33.520
Your suspicion is completely understandable.

09:33.520 --> 09:34.010
Huh?

09:34.590 --> 09:39.540
Well, if you ask me whether 
I have any suspicions or not, I do.

09:40.070 --> 09:40.970
However...

09:41.510 --> 09:43.740
I have a much bigger problem...

09:43.740 --> 09:46.520
While I can't take confessions,

09:46.910 --> 09:50.060
I can be helpful in giving advice.

09:50.490 --> 09:51.320
However...

09:52.690 --> 09:56.860
I can only give sincere advice when it 
doesn't revolve around making money.

09:58.340 --> 10:04.330
No, you're right. It may be better to 
ask someone like you in this situation.

10:04.330 --> 10:06.020
May I ask?

10:06.020 --> 10:09.230
Though, I'm not sure if I can 
give you a satisfactory answer.

10:11.480 --> 10:12.460
If...

10:13.020 --> 10:17.180
If the stories collected 
in that basement are true, then...

10:17.180 --> 10:18.010
Then?

10:18.340 --> 10:20.970
Does that mean the God we believe in is false?

10:21.900 --> 10:26.980
My father... Father Franz collected 
stories about the northern gods.

10:26.980 --> 10:31.370
He was suspected of heresy
 more than once or twice.

10:31.370 --> 10:35.530
Yet, he was a commendable priest 
who never missed a single day of prayer.

10:35.530 --> 10:42.530
However, if your companion is truly 
a pagan god, it would mean our God is false.

10:43.010 --> 10:44.680
I don't know.

10:44.680 --> 10:49.040
I do not have the courage to judge you 
with holy water and bible in hand.

10:49.370 --> 10:52.380
I can't even tell if my hesitation 
is good or bad thing...

10:52.380 --> 10:57.090
I am a mere traveling merchant, 
so I'm not well versed in the teachings of God.

10:57.410 --> 11:01.760
I can't really tell you what's right or wrong.

11:02.090 --> 11:06.520
However, I don't think Father Franz was wrong.

11:07.500 --> 11:08.990
Why...

11:08.990 --> 11:10.660
Why do you believe that?!

11:12.810 --> 11:14.610
That knock must be from elder Sem.

11:15.070 --> 11:17.230
He is probably here to speak to me about you.

11:18.770 --> 11:24.310
I will tell him that I've been asking you about 
the churches in other countries and towns.

11:25.260 --> 11:27.410
This isn't really a lie because...

11:27.410 --> 11:29.000
Yes, I understand.

11:29.450 --> 11:32.400
I would love to tell you about my experiences.

11:38.120 --> 11:39.970
You seemed quite compassionate.

11:39.970 --> 11:43.640
Merchants are always compassionate 
to those they do business with.

11:44.230 --> 11:46.860
Can you hear their conversation?

11:46.860 --> 11:49.100
She is speaking with him 
like she said she would.

11:49.440 --> 11:51.690
It seems the one named Sem 
is just about to leave.

11:51.690 --> 11:53.530
Our main problem is time.

11:53.530 --> 11:57.110
If we take too long, 
the snow will stop our travels.

11:57.410 --> 11:59.800
Yet, I do not know if we will 
get through all of this.

11:59.800 --> 12:03.820
I'm sure we'll be able to get through them 
if the two of us skim through quickly.

12:07.490 --> 12:08.470
Yes.

12:09.080 --> 12:09.980
What's wrong?

12:10.790 --> 12:13.370
I have told you that I am tired of being alone.

12:31.060 --> 12:35.020
The elder has returned home. 
About what we spoke of earlier...

12:41.160 --> 12:42.640
Then, let us speak again later.

12:50.620 --> 12:51.910
Hey, now.

12:56.920 --> 12:58.420
Did someone come to the church?

12:59.000 --> 13:00.920
I got it. It must be Evan.

13:03.530 --> 13:05.340
I have grown hungry.

13:05.680 --> 13:08.830
Well, let's take a break.

13:09.630 --> 13:12.060
Let's keep you a secret from Evan.

13:12.060 --> 13:14.940
Though that girl may tell him.

13:14.940 --> 13:18.900
She tells Evan how many times 
she sneezes in a day,

13:18.900 --> 13:22.640
but didn't tell him about 
when we first visited the church.

13:22.640 --> 13:24.950
I am still uneasy.

13:25.310 --> 13:29.150
We've also made a donation, 
I'm sure she understands what we mean.

13:29.150 --> 13:31.720
Most importantly, even if we 
can't trust the existence of god,

13:31.720 --> 13:34.120
we can trust those who are faithful to him.

13:34.120 --> 13:38.780
Yet, that girl seems quite troubled.

13:38.780 --> 13:41.590
Who knows what action she will take 
once she makes her decision?

13:42.600 --> 13:44.300
About God?

13:44.640 --> 13:47.450
Incidentally, how were you planning to reply?

13:47.450 --> 13:48.240
Oh...

13:48.540 --> 13:51.970
I think Father Franz started collecting 
stories about pagan gods

13:52.350 --> 13:55.390
to prove the existence of God.

13:56.520 --> 13:59.000
He prayed day after day, 
but never saw a hint of Him.

13:59.000 --> 14:03.400
It makes one want to question 
God's existence, doesn't it?

14:03.840 --> 14:07.500
Isn't that why he grew interested 
in the gods of others?

14:07.500 --> 14:09.780
If pagan gods truly exist...

14:09.780 --> 14:12.350
Then, there is no way God himself doesn't.

14:12.830 --> 14:14.290
God does not exist.

14:14.570 --> 14:16.780
After all, the Church believes that

14:16.780 --> 14:21.410
God created this world and that humans 
are merely borrowing it, correct?

14:21.410 --> 14:22.340
Yeah.

14:22.610 --> 14:26.110
Even so, I'm sure he wanted 
to feel His existence.

14:28.590 --> 14:30.430
Come, don't spill.

14:30.430 --> 14:32.300
And tear the bread before eating it.

14:32.300 --> 14:34.100
Yeah, I know.

14:34.580 --> 14:37.540
More importantly, 
please continue, Mr. Lawrence.

14:37.540 --> 14:39.040
Where was I?

14:39.040 --> 14:40.900
You just got on a large ship.

14:40.900 --> 14:42.580
Oh, that's right.

14:42.580 --> 14:45.360
The thing that surprised me 
most on the ship was the food.

14:45.360 --> 14:46.740
The food?

14:46.740 --> 14:47.490
Oh?

14:47.490 --> 14:50.240
There were merchants 
from many different regions.

14:50.240 --> 14:55.410
For instance, the bread of a merchant 
from the Ebgod region was incredibly salty.

14:55.410 --> 14:58.400
Salty bread? Can you believe it?

14:58.400 --> 14:59.490
Well...

14:59.490 --> 15:01.580
There was also completely flat bread.

15:01.890 --> 15:05.550
Flour and water were kneaded and baked before 
being blessed by the bread-leaving spirits.

15:05.980 --> 15:09.800
This one had honey in it and was really good.

15:11.410 --> 15:14.670
There are a lot of things I don't know 
about outside the village.

15:15.500 --> 15:19.060
Thank you very much for 
preparing such a feast today.

15:19.060 --> 15:23.730
No, you gave quite a generous donation. 
This is the least I can do.

15:24.050 --> 15:26.120
So, after this...

15:26.120 --> 15:28.400
You may read the books at night as well.

15:28.400 --> 15:29.690
Thank you.

15:29.690 --> 15:33.440
Then, Mr. Lawrence, tell me more 
about the outside world later!

15:33.440 --> 15:35.310
Evan, you need to practice writing.

15:35.310 --> 15:36.200
What?!

15:37.740 --> 15:38.540
Oh, that's right.

15:39.020 --> 15:40.890
About your question this afternoon...

15:40.890 --> 15:42.460
I will consider the answer on my own.

15:42.900 --> 15:47.630
Father Franz always said, think before asking.

15:49.050 --> 15:50.510
What are you talking about?

15:50.510 --> 15:51.550
It's nothing.

15:51.890 --> 15:54.340
Come on. Help me clean up.

15:54.870 --> 15:56.230
Sure thing.

15:58.030 --> 16:00.660
Not just the plates. Clean up the breadcrumbs.

16:00.660 --> 16:02.380
Yeah. Yeah. I got it.

16:02.380 --> 16:04.530
It's bad manners, so don't eat them.

16:04.530 --> 16:06.090
You don't have to tell me that.

16:06.090 --> 16:08.860
I wonder. You always seem so hungry, Evan.

16:11.820 --> 16:13.000
Those two...

16:13.000 --> 16:13.940
Yes?

16:13.940 --> 16:16.100
They get along really well.

16:19.910 --> 16:22.750
Huh? Did I same something odd?

16:22.750 --> 16:24.840
Well, you know...

16:24.840 --> 16:26.890
For the most part...

16:28.590 --> 16:32.320
I know my own good and bad points.

16:32.320 --> 16:33.390
Y-Yeah?

16:33.390 --> 16:34.810
So, you know...

16:34.810 --> 16:35.630
What's the matter?

16:35.630 --> 16:38.760
I wish you would not speak 
so enviously of them.

16:39.780 --> 16:41.090
I, too...

16:41.090 --> 16:43.050
No, I understand.

16:43.050 --> 16:44.520
I understand, but...

16:44.520 --> 16:47.360
We must look like quite the fools ourselves.

16:48.190 --> 16:52.400
I do not know why I feel 
so embarrassed about this.

16:52.720 --> 16:58.300
But you enviously say 
they get along well, yet we...

16:58.300 --> 16:58.830
No.

17:00.240 --> 17:06.040
No, well, you're right, but, I mean...

17:06.530 --> 17:08.790
No, I understand.

17:09.310 --> 17:10.710
I already knew.

17:11.010 --> 17:13.840
I just didn't want to put it into words.

17:14.220 --> 17:19.260
It's true that I'm envious, 
but not about their relationship.

17:20.610 --> 17:22.970
Those two will continue living in this church.

17:25.110 --> 17:26.230
But what about us?

17:27.070 --> 17:29.300
You found a clue about your hometown.

17:29.300 --> 17:32.130
And I'm helping you follow that clue.

17:32.130 --> 17:33.030
However,

17:34.660 --> 17:36.910
I'm a traveling merchant without any roots.

17:37.330 --> 17:38.490
You...

17:38.490 --> 17:39.380
So...

17:40.440 --> 17:43.950
What will you do once you return home?

17:51.190 --> 17:52.310
I do not know.

17:53.060 --> 17:56.470
A quick look at your hometown
 won't satisfying you, will it?

17:58.070 --> 17:59.510
No, let's not.

18:00.180 --> 18:01.340
I'm sorry.

18:01.340 --> 18:03.310
I am Wise Wolf Holo.

18:04.180 --> 18:06.270
I am Wise Wolf Holo of Yoitsu.

18:08.990 --> 18:11.300
I am Wise Wolf Holo of Yoitsu.

18:16.020 --> 18:16.640
What?

18:18.010 --> 18:18.660
Ho...

18:22.970 --> 18:24.370
Is there a problem?

18:24.860 --> 18:27.370
No, no problem...

18:32.510 --> 18:33.880
I shall sleep for a bit.

18:33.880 --> 18:36.480
Will you look through the books for me?

18:39.580 --> 18:41.270
All right.

18:57.400 --> 19:01.200
"I do not wish to regard the tale of this 
bear god as more special than others."

19:01.620 --> 19:05.700
"This god seems to be 
represented in various stories."

19:06.250 --> 19:10.000
<i>However, I believe this god is 
the only one I have been able</i>

19:10.000 --> 19:12.200
<i>to connect with others so thoroughly.</i>

19:12.200 --> 19:15.090
Does the Pope know of this?

19:15.380 --> 19:21.090
If my assumptions are correct, 
our God has triumphed without a fight.

19:21.370 --> 19:24.510
I cannot possibly remain calm if this is true.

19:24.770 --> 19:30.520
I could not help feeling strongly 
the existence of God as I assembled this book.

19:30.850 --> 19:35.770
"I hope that this will not be judged by 
narrow-minded worshipers of God,"

19:35.770 --> 19:41.800
"but those with open hearts whose love of 
God is like a gentle breeze in a vast field."

19:49.260 --> 19:51.680
I found a book about the Moon-Hunting Bear.

19:53.900 --> 19:55.080
Did something happen?

19:55.480 --> 19:57.210
There's a good chance.

19:59.980 --> 20:03.230
I don't know what you want 
to do after reading this.

20:03.880 --> 20:07.510
But I'd like you to be honest with me 
and tell me your thoughts.

20:09.720 --> 20:10.810
I understand.

20:11.970 --> 20:13.160
I promise.

20:25.980 --> 20:28.000
According to the letter on your desk,

20:28.000 --> 20:30.370
I thought Enberch wouldn't lay 
their hands on this village.

20:30.640 --> 20:34.050
The keen eyes of a merchant 
are truly impressive.

20:34.050 --> 20:35.880
That is what I thought myself...

20:36.140 --> 20:41.260
I'm a traveler. I can easily fall into 
danger when something happens.

20:41.260 --> 20:44.810
I will not allow anything like that 
to happen while I'm here.

20:44.810 --> 20:46.220
Please close up the basement.

20:46.220 --> 20:49.350
The elder will be sure to visit if this 
has something to do with Enberch.

20:50.250 --> 20:54.730
We stayed late into the night here 
after having a religious discussion.

20:54.730 --> 20:57.460
Since my companion is a nun, 
the situation is plausible.

20:58.130 --> 21:00.020
Take a blanket with you to the prayer room.

21:19.790 --> 21:21.390
However, as the village head...

21:29.710 --> 21:31.720
I apologize for disturbing you 
so late at night.

21:34.090 --> 21:35.020
Did something happen?

21:35.360 --> 21:38.270
Please bear with the inconvenience for now.

21:40.060 --> 21:43.110
I am a part of the Rowen Merchant Association.

21:44.070 --> 21:48.780
Many people in the Kumerson branch 
know that I am currently in this village.

21:49.460 --> 21:50.950
I understand.

21:51.970 --> 21:55.370
We have not appeared before you 
because we have ill intentions.

22:00.340 --> 22:04.550
Someone in Enberch has died 
